From cf8dcefcc3cefb620c4fc6985ca92a8323a6e585 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:08:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: enable the Raphael Venus codec

The pinned Raphael board declares QCOM_ID_SM8150 revision 0x20000,
so use the V2 resource graph instead of waiting on a silicon assumption
that the selected board profile already resolves. Preserve its existing
5 MiB firmware carveout at 0x97600000 and every audio/display fix.

Use the same case-sensitive board firmware directory as its other
remote processors. The Venus image must be installed as venus.mbn;
its presence, provenance and version remain a target preflight check,
not something a successful kernel build can establish.

Both codec children are created by the existing resource-driven
OF_DYNAMIC path (enabled by the Raphael configuration). This enables
both directions, not a declaration of successful hardware decoding or
encoding. Validate firmware authentication, both nodes, and H.264
round-trip tests before any stability claim.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
index f0028d363..a2916ade2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
@@ -1312,6 +1312,11 @@ &usb_1_hsphy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&venus {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/Xiaomi/raphael/venus.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &wifi {
 	vdd-0.8-cx-mx-supply = <&vdda_wcss_pll>;
 	vdd-1.8-xo-supply = <&vreg_pmu_xo>;
-- 
